\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10800\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\uc2 News\par \b \uc2 The Today Show for May 3, 2022, NBC\b0\par\par\uc2 Savannah Guthrie, Hoda Kotb, Craig Melvin, Al Roker, Carson Daly,  Sheinelle Jones, Pete Williams; Joe Fryer \par \uc2 7,430 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2022\par \uc2 NBC News: Today\par \uc2 TODA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and programming copyright 2022 NBCUniversal. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Transcription Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 [08:00:00]\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HODA KOTB, NBC NEWS TODAY, CO-ANCHOR: It is 8:00 on "TODAY." Coming up, Supreme Court stunner. A leaked draft opinion suggests the nation`s highest court is preparing to overturn Roe versus Wade. So, what would that decision mean for abortion in the U.S.? And how did this unprecedented leak take place? We`re live with the latest.\par \par \uc2 Then, remembering Naomi Judd. New details in the country music legend`s death as new tributes pour in. One from her friend Dolly Parton.\par \par \uc2 Plus, TikTok teacher. We are celebrating some incredible educators this morning. Including one Florida teacher using social media to liven up her lesson plan. So, you don`t want to miss the special surprises with have in store for all of them.\par \par \uc2 And red carpet ready. Some of the biggest celebrities step out for the annual Met Gala.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KARLIE KLOSS, FASHION MODEL: It`s magic. It`s like a fairytale.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: We`ll show you the can`t miss looks from fashion`s biggest night. Today, Tuesday, May 3, 2022.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CROWD: Hello Omaha, Nebraska.\par \par \uc2 CROWD: And Richville, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Celebrating my retirement.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: From St. Petersburg, Florida.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Here for Shiayan`s (ph) graduation.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: From Hagerstown, Maryland.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: First mother/son trip to New York.\par \par \uc2 CROWD: From Nashville.\par \par \uc2 CROWD: Good morning to our kids.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: In Topeka,\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: And Axtell, Kansas.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: From Plymouth, Massachusetts.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Celebrating mom`s birthday.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: From Huntsville, Alabama.\par \par \uc2 CROWD: Today is our 25th anniversary.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Happy anniversary. Happy everything. Welcome back to "TODAY" It`s a Tuesday morning. We love when you start your day with us. So, thank you.\par \par \uc2 CRAIG MELVIN, NBC NEWS ANCHOR: Yes.\par \par \uc2 SAVANNAH GUTHRIE, NBC NEWS TODAY, CO-ANCHOR: Finally getting a little springy out there on the plaza.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Finally.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Getting that --\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: -- little spring on our steps, too, guys.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Good to have you back, by the way.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Indeed.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: All right. We`re going to get right to our news at 8:00. A bombshell leak from the Supreme Court. Appears to suggest that the court is poised to strike down Roe versus Wade and federal protection for abortion rights. NBC`s Justice Correspondent Pete Williams has the latest on what is an apparent draft, not the opinion itself.\par \par \uc2 Hey, Pete, good morning.\par \par \uc2 PETE WILLIAMS, NBC NEWS JUSTICE CORRESPONDENT: Hoda, good morning. There is no way to confirm this and the Supreme Court isn`t commenting. But it`s almost certainly authentic because it was clear back in December when this case was argued that the court was preparing to overturn Roe V. Wade. Politico has now published the full of what it says it the draft opinion written by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 . And it says, "The inescapable conclusion is that the right to abortion is not deeply rooted in the nation`s history and traditions."\par \par \uc2 The court is considering the fate of a Mississippi law passed in 2018 but so far blocked by a lawsuit that would ban abortion after 15 weeks of pregnancy. Lower courts said it would violate the Supreme Court`s abortion precedence beginning with Roe in 1973 that say States cannot ban abortion before the age of fetal viability, that`s about 23 weeks into the pregnancy. If the Supreme Court does end up overruling Roe it would not make abortion illegal but it would allow each individual State to decide whether to ban it and about half the States have already said that they would. And this is remarkable for another reason, no one can remember a Supreme Court draft opinion leaking like this, especially in such a high- profile case. Hoda.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: All right. Pete Williams for us there at the Court House. Pete, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: We turn now to the three things to watch in Ukraine where Russian missiles struck the strategic Port City of Odessa overnight. Russia says it hit an airfield being used to transport sent by the West. Ukraine says the strikes took out a bridge and a school dormitory.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, some of the 100 civilians evacuated from that steel plant in Mariupol have started reaching Ukrainian-controlled territory. Russia continued to attack the plant where soldiers and other civilians have been trapped for weeks. And a senior U.S. diplomat is warning that Russia plans to annex much of Eastern Ukraine as early as this month.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Also, this morning, as the world mourns the loss of country music icon Naomi Judd. We are hearing more from the legend herself on her tireless crusade to raise awareness about mental health struggles. NBC News NOW Anchor Joe Fryer joins us with more.\par \par \uc2 Joe, good morning.\par \par \uc2 JOE FRYER, NBC NEWS NOW ANCHOR: Good morning. Music was Naomi Judd`s passion, but so was shining a light on mental health issues. The country music star was very open about her years-long battle with severe depression. Now, a new report says they have a cause for her death.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 FRYER (voiceover): This morning, new details in the death of country music legend Naomi Judd. People Magazine reports, the star died by suicide citing multiple anonymous sources. NBC News has not been able to confirm the cause of death.\par \par \uc2 [08:05:00]\par \par \uc2 Judd`s rep did not respond to our request for comments. On \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , Monday night, Ashley Judd posted a video of Naomi`s husband of more than 30 years, Larry Strickland honoring her memory through song.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, Ashley and Wynonna honored their mother as The Judds were inducted into the \uc2 Country Music Hall of Fame\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 WYNONNA JUDD, SINGER: It`s a very strange dynamic to be this broken and this blessed.\par \par \uc2 FRYER (voiceover): Naomi`s daughters announced they lost their mother to the disease of mental illness.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY JUDD, ACTRESS: And I`m sorry that she couldn`t hang on until today.\par \par \uc2 FRYER (voiceover): Other artists of the ceremony performed some of The Judd`s biggest hits. Fellow country icon Dolly Parton offered her condolences writing, Naomi and I were close. Just know that I will always love you. Naomi talked openly about her pain and her lifetime battle with depression speaking with Savannah in 2017.\par \par \uc2 NAOMI JUDD, SINGER: Savannah, I`m trying to start a national conversation about depression and anxiety because I may be just one little country singer right here, but there are 43 million who suffer from depression and anxiety.\par \par \uc2 FRYER (voiceover): A year later, she co-wrote a letter published in People calling for more research on suicide.\par \par \uc2 N. JUDD: The only time I don`t feel afraid or lonely or fearful is when I`m up on that stage.\par \par \uc2 FRYER (voiceover): Those were Naomi`s words just last month before taking the stage with her daughter at the CMT Music Awards. We now know it would be her final performance.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 FRYER (on camera): CMT plans to honor Naomi Judd. That performance of "Love Can Build a Bridge" will air every hour during the music hours on all of CMT`s channels this week. And tonight, the network will air a half-hour special on her life and legacy. Back to you, guys.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: All right. Joe Fryer for us. Joe, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: The British army is investigating what would be a shocking royal security breach. An intruder reportedly posed as a priest and spent a night in the barracks of troops who guard Queen Elizabeth at Windsor Castle. Two UK news organizations reporting the imposter ate and drank with senior officers before spending the night. Police were called the next morning and he was removed. Queen Elizabeth who celebrates her platinum jubilee next month was not staying at the Windsor Castle when the alleged intrusion took place.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: All right. It is seven minutes after the hour. Are you all ready for a boost?\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Yes, ma`am.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: OK. Here we go. Here we go. The highlight of even a well-planned wedding is sometimes a moment that nobody planned at all. Even when the ring boy sees his mom in her wedding gown.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Hi, ma.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Two-year-old Pierceson (ph) who turns three tomorrow, by the way, his mom said that moment that he ran up to her was so precious. She could have gone home right then. But don`t you love how little kid can run with his arms outstretched.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: That`s sweet. I love --\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Oh, yes.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Like that just happens.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: I love how he`s running down the aisle. That`s so sweet.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Awesome.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Gosh.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Beautiful.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Well, coming up next. Sheinelle was hanging with the stars last night. She hit the red carpet at fashion`s biggest and most exclusive party of the year, the Met Gala, right after this.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [08:10:00]\par \par \uc2 KOTB: We`re back at 8:13 with the super bowl of fashion. Of course, we`re talking about the Met Gala.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Yes, the biggest stars stepped out in their finest here in New York City last nigh