 Goldberg (ph), Tammy Chaine (ph), Ama O`Neill, Lisette Torres (ph) and Natalie Stuart, they all work on the (inaudible) --\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yes. Ms. Stuart is a 3rd grade teacher at Nova Dwight Eisenhower Elementary School. And if you recognize her, and I think a lot of people do, because she`s a TikTok sensation.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: All right. So let`s go check out why her students think she deserves an A plus.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 NATALIE STUART, TEACHER, NOVA DWIGHT EISENHOWER ELEMENTARY SCHOOL: And I love that while I`m only a part of a child`s life for 10 months in their whole life, it`s amazing how in those 10 months I can make a difference that will last a lifetime.\par \par \uc2 By now you should already have the process of elimination flowing here. Rectangle A is correct. (Inaudible) that`s beautiful. Yes. What two numbers multiplied can give you 12?\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE (voice-over): Natalie Stuart is a 3rd grade teacher at Nova Dwight Eisenhower Elementary School just outside of Fort Lauderdale, and it`s no surprise she`s their Teacher of the Year.\par \par \uc2 She started posting on TikTok during the pandemic to help keep her students engaged. But it wasn`t just the students who noticed this post, it racked up over 22 million views.\par \par \uc2 STUART: Y`all, I`ll tell you what I want what I really, really want.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED SPEAKERS: I`ll tell you what I want what I really, really want.\par \par \uc2 STUART: Here we go.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE (voice-over): Now, TicTok is a regular part of connecting with our class, posting Friday dances.\par \par \uc2 NIGINE TYGHTER, PRINCIPAL, NOVA DWIGHT EISENHOWER ELEMENTARY SCHOOL: This story is a one of a kind, right there`s a let me really engage connect with my students and meet them where they are.\par \par \uc2 STUART: I`ll hear students tell me I want to be in your class next year. You have so much fun. And then they`ll tell me when they`re in here. Ma`am, we work a lot.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE (voice-over): Her classroom decor includes some of her favorites, from Jedis to Jimmy Fallon. And when it comes to academics, she gets an A from parents.\par \par \uc2 ARTINA ROBINSON, PARENT: Ms. Stuart knows how to teach a certain skill that maybe I as a parent can`t teach my child.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Well, she`ll make it fun instead of making a boring.\par \par \uc2 STUART: And the area is 30 squared unit, correct.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED SPEAKERS: Yehey.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I appreciate Ms. Stuart a lot. My child`s teacher has her back as well as I do, so that`s wonderful.\par \par \uc2 STUART: You have three minutes and 41 seconds. And the song is "We Don`t Talk About Bruno."\par \par \uc2 Over time, I thought why not include the celebrity in what I do.\par \par \uc2 Someone is joining our lesson today, and it is Pauly D.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED SPEAKERS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE (voice-over): So, she glued celebrities to popsicle sticks as her teacher assistants.\par \par \uc2 Stuart: One of our favorite teacher assistants is Pauly D. The kids love screaming, yes, buddy.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes, buddy.\par \par \uc2 STUART: That`s right.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE (voice-over): Ms. Stuart teaches in a Title 1 school, the majority of students are underprivileged living in low income areas. Even her former students now in high school say her impact goes beyond the classroom.\par \par \uc2 MELANIE LIBURD, FORMER STUDENT: Mr. Stuart is my favorite teacher to this day. It`s nice to go back and volunteer.\par \par \uc2 TRISTAN NICHOLS, STUDENT: Ms. Stuart, if you`re watching, we love you.\par \par \uc2 [08:40:05]\par \par \uc2 ALAYNA CRAWFORD, STUDENT: Thank you, Ms. Stuart, for being the best teacher we ever had and making us do fun things while we work.\par \par \uc2 ALEX CASTRO, STUDENT: I really love you. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED SPEAKERS: We love you, Ms. Stuart.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Natalie, ooh.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Go, Natalie.\par \par \uc2 STUART: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: You are loved and adored by the students by your fellow teachers who by the way were weeping watching you. How does it feel to receive all of that?\par \par \uc2 STUART: Priceless. There`s no price. And honestly, like my kids, I love them so much. They`re -- what makes my day just so bright and every day is a new day with them, everyday is a fun day with them. And honestly, my colleagues who are here with me today are my backbone. They`re here for me in good times, bad times. They teach me new things. They guide me, they support me, and I`m just blessed.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: You guys have blessed us with your presence this morning. And, Sheinelle, where are you? Skate on over, Sheinelle.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Come on, Sheinelle.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Because we`ve got some fun for, y`all.\par \par \uc2 SHEINELLE JONES, NBC ANCHOR: Hi, Natalie. How are you, guys, this morning? Hey, so here`s the deal, Natalie. We heard the last past few weeks have been a little rough for you. I know you had some trouble with your car. It ended up breaking literally, burning down. In fact I want people take a look at this monitor.\par \par \uc2 STUART: Yes.\par \par \uc2 JONES: You guys recognize this place? Well, Carvana heard your story and wanted to help you out. That Toyota Four Runner, look at this, that you see right her in your driveway as we speak. Well now, guess what? You are the proud owner.\par \par \uc2 I love it, OK. So wait a minute. OK. But before we go, though, we also want to celebrate all of you guys, fellow teachers. You`ve all joined this celebration about what`s so hard and you all deserve a little break, right?\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yes.\par \par \uc2 JONES: So here`s the deal. Would you like to go on vacation?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Amara Cay Resort in Islamorada, Florida, they`ve decided they want to give each of you a three night stay. All get to bring a guest so you don`t have to go alone. Again, we`re not finished, you`ll receive $200 of daily resort credits. And that`s not all, to help you get there, they`re gifting you with a $100 gas gift card. So you guys are on your way.\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Savannah, the girls weekend.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Girls weekend, right?\par \par \uc2 STUART: Oh my god.\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Thank you, guys.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Y`all, so we love you.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 STUART: Oh my god. I cannot believe this.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: We love y`all so much.\par \par \uc2 JONES: The teachers make the world go round. We wouldn`t be here we out the teachers, so God bless you and all the teachers watching. God bless you, guys, too.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Thank you, thank you, thank you. And if you`re at home and you ever New York, don`t forget to come down to the roller rink. Y`all can skate here. You know what, I`m joining the skating (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: All right, yes. Come down and play with us.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Does it bringing back memories?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: Yes, right?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes, yes.\par \par \uc2 GUTHRIE: OK. Well, just ahead, we`ve got a Broadway show on our plaza, roll on over there and check it out. We`re going to channel pop icons and some famous figures from history, this amazing new Broadway show "Six" and we get a sneak preview (inaudible). But first, this is Today on NBC.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [08:46:30]\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The Citi Music Series on Today is proudly presented to you by Citi.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: We are back with more of the 