ft interior. So, those teeth are going to grab onto that exterior and allow you to get really beautiful slices.\par \par \uc2 JONES: That is the best looking tomato I`ve seen out here.\par \par \uc2 BESSER: Right. The season is upon us. All we need is some toast with a little mayo, maybe bacon. And then, you can use the top to pick it up and put it on your sandwich.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Look at that.\par \par \uc2 BESSER: Wherever you need them. But I love it.\par \par \uc2 JONES: OK.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: We`ve got a couple of these at the house. I love these things.\par \par \uc2 BESSER: OK. The peeler is the best.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 BESSER: This is the peeler that all restaurant kitchens use. It is a Y peeler. And the reason why we love the Y peeler is because it gives you so much more -- why do we love the Y?\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Why?\par \par \uc2 BESSER: It`s because it gives you so much more control over your produce.\par \par \uc2 JONES: OK.\par \par \uc2 [09:55:00]\par \par \uc2 BESSER: So, I like using this for any kitchen thing that you could possibly could want. But it is also really great for cheese, if you want to grate some parm over the top of a salad. And it also comes with a little tiny thing right here to remove any eyes in potatoes. Yes, so you can just scoop on it.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Here is a question, Elena. Maybe I could catch you off guard here.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Not going to stop him though.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: When you -- like an apple or something like that, if you accidentally eat the label. Are you OK?\par \par \uc2 BESSER: You know, I would say -- you shouldn`t trust me on that, I don`t necessarily know. I feel like --\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Is that something that`s happening frequently in your house?\par \par \uc2 ROKER: That`s happened once or twice.\par \par \uc2 BESSER: Why?\par \par \uc2 JONES: You should slow down.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Sometimes it`s what happens.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Sorry, Elena.\pa