ught than the cat movie. It should be reel.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: You know what? Maybe you`re a dog person.\par \par \uc2 GEIST: Kept this up.\par \par \uc2 SYLVESTER: William Russell Geist, you have a chance of coming back.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Oh, wow, you did some research.\par \par \uc2 GEIST: Wow! You did -- you did your research.\par \par \uc2 SYLVESTER: My mother is in love with Willie. Hey, mom. There`s Willie.\par \par \uc2 GEIST: Hi, mom. Hi, mom.\par \par \uc2 SYLVESTER: Writing Around the Christmas Tree.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: He knows (INAUDIBLE).\par \par \uc2 SYLVESTER: When successful novelist Mikaela decides to revive her deceased mother`s annual holiday writer`s retreat at her father`s snowy chic chalet, she soon meets handsome yet opinionated, non-fiction writer Levi, and a romance ignites between them.\par \par \uc2 GEIST: I think we`ve had too many unreal in a row.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: It`s reel.\par \par \uc2 GEIST: So, I`m going at reel.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: It`s reel.\par \par \uc2 GEIST: Yes.\par \par \uc2 SYLVESTER: You know what, I love lifetime. It is reel.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Yes, of course it is.\par \par \uc2 SYLVESTER: Everybody --\par \par \uc2 HAGER: OK, yes, it did. But I like -- I kind of want to see them.\par \par \uc2 GEIST: Yes, I thought, it`s a good movie. Yes, I`d watch that.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: OK.\par \par \uc2 SYLVESTER: This one might be based on a true story. This one might be based on a real true story. Single All the Way. Desperate to avoid his family`s judgment about being single, Peter persuades his best friend Nick to pose as his boyfriend. On a trip home for the holidays.\par \par \uc2 This might be based on my life.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Is -- are you -- does -- bringing tears?\par \par \uc2 SYLVESTER: Is it reel or unreal? Yes, that`s tears.\par \par \uc2 GEIST: I mean --\par \par \uc2 SYLVESTER: Single All the Way.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: I have now you`re confusing us with the --\par \par \uc2 GEIST: But that title