l`s tracking it all live.\par \par \uc2 Breast cancer breakthrough?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DR. G. THOMAS BUDD, CLEVELAND CLINIC MEDICAL ONCOLOGIST: If we could prevent 12 to 15 percent of breast cancer and the most deadly type, it would be a major step.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: The new vaccine to prevent one of the most aggressive forms of breast cancer. Why this early study has doctors hopeful. Just ahead, how the trial will work and what researchers are hoping to see.\par \par \uc2 And live in Studio 1A, Lady A stops by to talk about their latest album and give us a performance. Plus, we will catch up with Chrissy Teigen after a challenging year, and taste test recipes from her new cookbook.\par \par \uc2 TODAY, Tuesday, October 26, 2021.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Hello from Vadnais Heights Elementary School.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We`re coming to you from White Bear Lake, Minnesota. Go, Bears.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Hi, I`m Lauren.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: And I`m Julie.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Roses are red. Violets are blue. And we hope you love Halloween as much as we do. Happy Halloween.\par \par \uc2 BOYS: Hi, TODAY show.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED BOY: We`re the Tomkins (ph).\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: From Camillus, New York.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Today we`re celebrating --\par \par \uc2 BOY: My brother Carter`s 11th birthday.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Hi, this is Kelly and John from St. Petersburg, Florida, and we`re here to celebrate Ila`s second birthday.\par \par \uc2 Say hi, Hoda.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED GIRL: Hi, Hoda.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Happy birthday. Two looks good.\par \par \uc2 Welcome back to TODAY. We`re so happy that you`re joining us. It`s a Tuesday morning.\par \par \uc2 Craig is on assignment. Tom`s here.\par \par \uc2 It`s a soaker, ain`t it?