 Back to you.\par \par \uc2 STEPANOVA: All right, Matt. Still busy on the roads as well, crash inside the O`Neill Tunnel, still blocking two lanes an hour back to the Braintree. Split heavy delays here by the gas tank and other accident as you travel the Pike. Westbound by Route 16 and 128 North by Route 2, and a slow ride on Route 1 approaching Route 68 Copeland Circle. Those delays all the way back into Peabody. See you again at 11:00.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and programming copyright 2021 NBCUniversal.  ALL RIGHTS   RESERVED. Transcription Copyright 2021 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document TODA000020211026ehaq000gp\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 The Growing Tributes To Halyna Hutchins, The Pioneering Cinematographer Who Was Killed\b0\par\par\uc2 Hoda Kotb, Craig Melvin, Savannah Guthrie, Erin Mclaughlin \par \uc2 8,174 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 October 2021\par \uc2 NBC News: Today\par \uc2 TODA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and programming copyright 2021 NBCUniversal. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Transcription Copyright 2021 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 [10:00:18]\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SHANNON WEST, FROM WEST SAINT PAUL, MINNESOTA: Hi! This is Shannon from West Saint Paul, Minnesota with my puppy Maddox. We love sitting outside on these fall mornings, enjoying this beautiful weather watching Hoda and Jenna.\par \par \uc2 HODA KOTB, NBC NEWS HOST (voice-over): Coming up.\par \par \uc2 Emmy-winning actress Uzo Aduba. Find out what she`s doing to kick off her next chapter.\par \par \uc2 Plus, Grammy winner Sheryl Crow opens up about the biggest challenges in her life and the biggest joys.\par \par \uc2 And get ready for your mind to be blown when The Clairvoyants pull a couple of tricks out of their bag.\par \par \uc2 Right now.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER: From NBC News, this is "TODAY" with Hoda Kotb and Jenna Bush Hager from Studio 1A in Rockefeller Plaza.\par \par \uc2 KOTB (on camera): Come on. Welcome in. It`s Monday. It`s October the 25th. We`re so happy you`re sharing this day with us. This is "All I Wanna Do" by Sheryl Crow.\par \par \uc2 Jenna, first of all, we love her.\par \par \uc2 JENNA BUSH HAGER, NBC NEWS HOST: Yes.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Secondly, I got a chance to sit with her and visit. And I realized as I was sitting with her that I don`t really know that much about her.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Other than her music part. So, we have a really interesting and fun conversation.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: And y`all actually have a lot in common. Did you leave thinking you wanted her to be your friend?\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yes, bestie. And by the way, she has a big birthday coming up. She`s turning 60. And she - it was -- she has such a great way of a great outlook on everything. She`s putting out new music. She`s got kids that are like 11 and 14. And she`s living her life. But we`ll talk more about that.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Can`t wait to hear more of that. And a shoutout to our friend Shannon from Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Hey, Shannon.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: She`s having fun with her pup Maddox. Thank you so much for sharing how you watch our show and keep those videos coming to hodaandjenna.com.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: OK. So, this was a big "Saturday Night Live." Everyone was waiting for Jason Sudeikis.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Jason Sudeikis.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: And do you remember when we were going to try to go together and then I couldn`t because I was going away. Well, anyway, we`ll get to that in a second.\par \par \uc2 So, Jason started off "SNL" with a beautiful sentimental monologue. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Uh-oh.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JASON SUDEIKIS, ACTOR: The thing about all the brilliance that`s happened in here, all your favorite sketches, wild and crazy guys, Gilly and Cowbell, Wayne`s World, all happened. Right here, in here, where you are. This place changed my life, twice, twice. Once as a cast member, as a writer here but most importantly as a kid watching from home, you know. And there`s a good chance that if you`re watching tonight, there`s probably something from this place that probably change your life, too, right? And I`ll tell you this. If this is your first time watching this show, well, I mean -- well, this one probably won`t change your life.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: OK.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: I like him so much.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: You were there?\par \par \uc2 HAGER: I was there.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: How did they like --\par \par \uc2 HAGER: And I like Jason Sudeikis so much.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Wait, wait. Was it kind -- you and Savannah again?\par \par \uc2 Kind of like the U.S. Open? Is this a repeat?\par \par \uc2 Wait. You and Savannah went together?\par \par \uc2 HAGER: I asked --\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Wait. The whole group?\par \par \uc2 HAGER: I asked you and Joel.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Wait. Is Brad Pitt on the other side of you?\par \par \uc2 Oh, my word.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: I asked you and Joel if you could go and you said yes. And then you cancled.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Well, no. I didn`t cancel.\par \par \uc2 I was going - I went to Rehoboth to see my mom but it sounds like it`s a really chummy foursome.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Gavin asked me for pictures. And Gavin, what did I say? I said, no, thank you. I don`t want to hurt Hoda`s feelings.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Oh.\par \par \uc2 GAVIN SHULMAN, SUPERVISING PRODUCER, NBC NEWS "TODAY" SHOW: And then eventually sent them.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: And then eventually sent them was the follow up.\par \par \uc2 By the way, I have to say, one of the things I love about Jenna is this right now. This.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Well, I wanted to go with you.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Because you`re so sweet that you don`t want to hurt my feelings. I remember when I went to you, when you came to me and you were like, I want to tell you some good news, but I don`t want to hurt your feelings. I was like, what is it? You`re like I`m pregnant. Because you knew that I wanted to adopt. And you were crying telling me about your beautiful pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: I was so scared.\par \par \uc2 You were like, do you not want to do this show?\par \par \uc2 And I was like, no, I want to do this show but I`m pregnant.\par \par \uc2 And you were like -\par \par \uc2 KOTB: I was so happy.\par \par \uc2 And then you were like, because I know you`re waiting. That`s who you are. That`s why this is beautiful. That`s why I tease you. I love you.\par \par \uc2 But tell me about Jason Sudeikis.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: OK. First of all, I have a thing for Jason Sudeikis.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yes. What is it about him?\par \par \uc2 HAGER: It`s because he`s so earnest and kind.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: And kind in real life, too. I bet.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: In real life.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: OK.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: That`s him. That`s his monologue. That was him.\par \par \uc2 So, I - but I was with my husband. So, I didn`t tell him that.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yeah, yeah. You couldn`t.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: But he was so good. He was in "What`s Up with That?"\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Oh, "What`s Up with That."\par \par \uc2 HAGER: "What`s Up with That"\par \par \uc2 He did the dancing man.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: I love the dancing man.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: And then Brandi Carlile who --\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Oh, wait. Want to see a little?\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO PLAYS "WHAT`S UP WITH THAT" ON "SATURDAY NIGHT LIVE")\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Oh my God. Is that Kenny G? OK. That`s hilarious.\par \par \uc2 [10:05:00]\par \par \uc2 HAGER: And then there was - he did everything.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: What character?\par \par \uc2 HAGER: He was in every single skit. I loved the melon which is the man "Ellen."\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Oh, the man "Ellen."\par \par \uc2 Oh, was it so -\par \par \uc2 HAGER: It was so weird. But I was talking about if they just did a show for men. So, they were like -\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Oh, like an "Ellen" for men?\par \par \uc2 HAGER: -- then, we`ll give you towels. And you`ll start spanking each other. Like just bizarre. But it was so much fun.\par \par \uc2 And he also brought back "The Devil."\par \par \uc2 Do we have any clips of this?\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Do we clips of anything, maybe not?\par \par \uc2 HAGER: No. Hoda wasn`t there.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Oh wait. I want to see.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO PLAYS "THE DEVIL" ON "SATURDAY NIGHT LIVE")\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Oh.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Don`t you love that?\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Love, love, love.\par \par \uc2 How about Brandi -\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Brandi Carlile.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Do you love her?\par \par \uc2 HAGER: I love Brandi Carlile so much and do not be confused with Belinda Carlisle.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: This -- she is incredible.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Oh yeah. I love Brandi Carlile.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: You have to listen to her new album.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Remember - she had the book out, right?\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: The book called "Broken Horses." I got to talk with her a little bit. But y`all, if you want new music today, download Brandi Carlile`s new album. It`s so good.\par \par \uc2 Gavin, has your wife been listening to it?\par \par \uc2 SHULMAN: She loves it.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: She loves it.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: There`s a man yelling behind his mask. She loves it.\par \par \uc2 That`s really cool though. Really cool. What a great night.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: All right. Will you talk about your weekend?\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yeah, it was fine.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, my weekend was great. Jenna, I went to visit -- we went to visit my mom and my sister in Rehoboth Beach. And we decided since we were all going to be together and we weren`t going to be together for Halloween that we should dress up in our outfits. So, the girls, Haley was a unicorn and Hope was a puppy and I was a sun, and my sister was a star, and my mom was the moon.\par \par \uc2 So, anyway, we got out there. And we`re like, well, we might as well go see if anyone is available for candies, so we started knocking on doors.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Wait.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Nobody.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: What happens when Hoda stands at somebody`s door?\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Wait a second. On the third door, a lady named Becky looked startled. She goes, what, it was just my name is Becky. And I go, we go trick or treat. She was like, oh, God. So, she goes, I think I have something. She ran in the house. She came out. She had two Reese`s cups, one for Haley and one for Hope. And it was like -- it was awesome. We were laughing about it. Should we knock on that door? Should we knock on that door? But we had such a great - it was just fun.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: I mean, only you do kind of bizarre things.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: We`re all together.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: It`s super sweet.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: OK. And here`s the photo that you posted on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: By the way, it`s listed with a few comments. Starting with, "Doesn`t everyone need a heads up before we start trick or treating."\par \par \uc2 Followed with one person just writing, "Why???"\par \par \uc2 And then this one is a great idea. "We went, one year, the day after. So many people wanted to get rid of their candy!"\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Oh, that`s so brilliant.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Isn`t that hilarious?\par \par \uc2 KOTB: So, what do you guys do on Halloween Day? Like -\par \par \uc2 HAGER: So, Halloween Day, we like to go really early in New York City.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Really? Like what, four?\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Like four. Right? Early. We go trick or treating.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: And then what we sometimes do, some of our friends in the neighborhood, we meet at a little local restaurant.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Savannah?\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 I just wondered. No, but Savannah and Vale and Charlie.\par \par \uc2 OK. And then your girl and boy.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: You forgot about Hal.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: I said boy, and boy.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: OK. So, then we meet at a restaurant at like -- you want to come? Do you want to come?\par \par \uc2 KOTB: It`s OK.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Please, come. Anybody is invited.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: By the way, you`re the sweetest person on the planet earth. I`m just letting you know. I`m just reiterating the sweetest person on the planet earth. You really are.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Can we move on to Steve Harvey?\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yes, yes. Let`s move on.\par \par \uc2 Steve Harvey is having a renaissance. It`s like an awakening.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: OK.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: A physical awakening.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: It`s a fashion awakening because evidently his wife -- his wife first said I don`t like the way you dress.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Wow.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: To him.\par \par \uc2 Was that his old way of dressing?\par \par \uc2 KOTB: I think that was the old way.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: OK.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: So, that was the old way which looks very, you know, dapper.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Dapper.\par \par \uc2 Whoa!\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Look at him now. Can you stand it? Look at the green parka.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Look at his leather pants.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: And look at the blue, bright blue jacket and look at the long coat.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: I mean, also, he`s wearing --\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Marjorie knows what she`s doing.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: OK. So, Marjorie - yeah, his wife Marjorie and Steve`s stylist, Elly, they went to work on his wardrobe.\par \par \uc2 Is that lavender?\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Oh, my gosh. Most guys can`t pull that off.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: No, no.\par \par \uc2 So, they just changed everything for him.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: They just totally changed it up.\par \par \uc2 What would Henry -- how would he react if you were like --\par \par \uc2 HAGER: If I brought out some leather pants?\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 If I held up some leather pants for Henry, he would be like am I going as Ozzy Osbourne for Halloween which he has done one year.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: He did?\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 I mean, what if you held up some leather pants for Joel?\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Well, Joel wears cargo shorts, flip flops until it snows and a sweatshirt. That`s what he likes. And you know what, he looks cool in that. He`s comfortable. He likes that.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Cargo shorts, flip flops. He`s kind of got Carson`s style.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Yeah. There he is.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yeah. We look totally -\par \par \uc2 HAGER: In a T-shirt.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: We`re so happy.\par \par \uc2 But that`s it.\par \par \uc2 What`s - how would you describe Henry`s style?\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Henry kind of likes - like a jean, sort of jean on jean, kind of western belt look.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Jean on jean?\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Jean on jean western belt.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Oh, I like that.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: But he was like even getting ready for "Saturday Night Live," he said, I thought -- like he came out in a shirt that was so short that had stains on it. He`s like this is cool, right, like in downtown?\par \par \uc2 [10:10:00]\par \par \uc2 I`m like, it`s cool but there`s stains on the shirt. Maybe we should give our guys -\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Makeover. No, I don`t think so.\par \par \uc2 Do you?\par \par \uc2 HAGER: I`m kind of into it.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Goodbye, flip flops.\par \par \uc2 All right. If you love reading as much as Jenna, there`s something that you may be crazy about.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Yeah. Three-time Emmy winner Uzo Aduba. She`s going to tell us all about her awesome new show. Coming up after this.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 KOTB: How many of you know Uzo Aduba as "Crazy Eyes" from "Orange is the New Black?" But did you know before it was a hit show, "Orange is the New Black" was actually a memoir.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Yes. Now, Uzo is teaming up with \uc2 Netflix\uc2  on a project that readers will love. I just love this. They`re bringing other stories from the page to the screen.\par \par \uc2 Uzo, it`s so nice to see you.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Bring her in. Can you guys bring Uzo in? Bring her in.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Bring Uzo in.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Bring her in, guys.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: We have you on the screen.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Bring her in.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: We`re bringing you in on screen.\par \par \uc2 We want you here though.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Uzo, wait. Here it is.\par \par \uc2 [10:15:00]\par \par \uc2 The grand entrance. Wait a second.\par \par \uc2 HAGER: Uzo.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: Yes! You know what, Uzo, that`s how you make an entrance.\par \par \uc2 UZO ADUBA, ACTRESS: Hi, ladies.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: How are you?\par \par \uc2 ADUBA: I`m great. How are you?\par \par \uc2 KOTB: By the way, so much - OK.\par \par \uc2 ADUBA: It`s great to see you guys again.\par \par \uc2 KOTB: You go away for a little bit and then you come back. And all of the sudden, there`s