ists, you think, oh, this is -- you`re going to write, you`re --\par \par \uc2 JONES: Be creative.\par \par \uc2 PULLMAN: You`re going to be creative.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PULLMAN: You`re going to get that one person`s show going. Nothing like that happened. You know, I just want able to really, though, enjoy just getting to do work, physical work, you know, and --\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: Let`s talk about your hobby. In addition to the ranch, Bill Pullman makes cider. Who knew?\par \par \uc2 PULLMAN: Well, it`s -- this turned out to be a little different thing than I thought when I brought it here. This is just for you guys.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Oh, we`ll take it. Tell us about this. I mean, I don`t know anyone else who makes cider.\par \par \uc2 PULLMAN: Well, you know, I have a -- my older brothers and sisters in Western New York State, we have wild apples. And then, this friend of mine, who is a -- is a consultant, he has a business doing cider called Cider Creek. But he -- we use his facility and his expertise and we just do kind of cooperative for --\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Is it kind of a hard cider?\par \par \uc2 PULLMAN: It`s very much a hard cider.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Oh, yes. That`s why we love Bill Pullman, ladies and gentlemen. And by the way, happy 25th anniversary, "Independence Day."\par \par \uc2 PULLMAN: Oh, yes.\par \par \uc2 JONES: Has it been 25?\par \par \uc2 ROKER: 25 years.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: That`s crazy, 25 years.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: One of the greatest presidential speeches ever.\par \par \uc2 MELVIN: That`s true.\par \par \uc2 PULLMAN: Oh, well, I heard from the stage manager that you watched the movie on 4th of July.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Constantly. Constantly. That`s one of our traditions. Got to do it. Thank you, sir.\par \par \uc2 JONES: I love it.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 JONES: You are a delight. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 ROKER: Hey. The fourth season of "The Sinner" premiering O